content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal drip of approximately 1 drop/second: no numerical permissible seal-leakage rate is documented. The applicable manual criterion is the symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check; the reported drip is therefore actionable rather than an accepted normal value.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.4 mm/s: the applicable HF-300 limit chart uses mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. On that scale, 3.4 falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'), below Zone C (4.5–7.1) and the highest-severity Zone D (from 7.1). It therefore does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop requirement, subject to confirming that the field reading uses the chart's RMS and bearing-housing measurement basis.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature of 70 C: applying the bearing-housing surface temperature limits, 70 C is at the upper end of 'Normal up to 70 C', below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Because the reading is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07's requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First check for early failure of the superseded HF3-450 component seal, if that seal is currently installed. The bulletin attributes early failures on HF-300 pumps built from serial HF3-22000 to a revised sleeve tolerance, and P-104's serial HF3-22871 is within the affected range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented causes of shaft-seal leakage are worn or cracked seal faces, the seal having run dry, and shaft misalignment. Confirm the seal condition, dry-run/flush history and alignment rather than assuming the serial-related failure is the only possible cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before intrusive work, isolate and drain the pump using the electrical LOTO, suction/discharge mechanical isolation, drain-and-vent and line-break permit controls listed in safety_controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly using the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment, then remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve. Record the installed seal part number and inspect the sleeve for scoring; replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket; do not fit HF3-450 on this pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting, but the sleeve-scoring inspection and conditional sleeve replacement still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with lightly oiled threads. Tighten the M10 seal gland nuts to 30 Nm for HF3-450B. For other applicable fasteners, use Table 5: M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts 210 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as part of the leakage corrective action. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing; applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, ensure the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is available and do not run the seal dry. No numerical post-repair leakage acceptance criterion is provided; see open_questions.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required replacement for this serial range. Do not fit the superseded HF3-450 component seal.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket during mechanical-seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve: have one available and install it only if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within P-101 to P-106 on the chemically dosed filtered-water line, which uses sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current reported vibration is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. As a restart/operations contingency, if vibration is subsequently confirmed in Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician; include it for the alignment check and apply section 5.4 whenever the motor or bearing housing is moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies HF3-450 and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 requires HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, specifically applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; P-104 is HF3-22871, so the bulletin governs this asset. Fit HF3-450B and use 30 Nm. The previous-shift instruction to ignore the bulletin and use 25 Nm for all pumps does not apply. Only pumps below serial HF3-22000 continue with HF3-450 and the manual's Table 5 seal arrangement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently installed—HF3-450 or HF3-450B—and is there any history of dry running or previous seal replacement?",
    "Does shaft sleeve HF3-455 have scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth? This determines whether the conditional sleeve is installed.",
    "Was the 3.4 mm/s vibration reading measured as RMS on a bearing housing, as required by Figure 3, and at which bearing housing? The Zone B classification is provisional until that measurement basis is confirmed.",
    "Was the 70 C reading taken on a bearing-housing surface, and which housing was measured? The supplied normal, alarm and trip limits apply to bearing-housing surface temperature.",
    "No numerical allowable seal-leakage rate, post-repair leakage acceptance criterion or maximum run-before-repair interval is supplied. Obtain engineering/reliability direction if continued operation before repair is proposed.",
    "The supplied documents define the priority-1 temperature trigger but do not define P2/P3 response times or a completion deadline for this active seal leak; the planner must confirm the required due date.",
    "No standard times are supplied for isolation/permitting, sleeve replacement or additional diagnostic work beyond the listed seal-replacement and laser-alignment tasks."
  ]
}
